## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | IMPORTANT | flutter_app/lib/ui/widgets/file_browser.dart | ⚠️ important childpath doesn t follow the segmentsabsolute fix — file open and upload still resolve against the env cwd the new absolute path handling fixes listdir envpath keeps the leading slash but the sibling path builder used for every non listing operation still drops it childpath file browser dart 415 returns the bare joined segments with no leading slash and no segmentsabsolute branch dart string childpath string name final joined segments isempty name segments join name return navigatesmountnamespace projectmountsegment joined joined in the exact state this pr fixes direct access host browser env rooted elsewhere folder outside cwd and outside any mount — the state the new direct access lists an absolute session folder outside the env cwd test models tapping a file → filepreviewscreen inline preview reads users x proj a txt relative to the env cwd → could not load file · no such file or directory upload → writebinaryfile childpath name … file browser dart 686 silently lands in the env cwd the session folder instead of the displayed folder — the same wrong destination class the gh 2131 comments below childpath describe fixing for the mount namespace mirror the absolute handling this is the same one line contract envpath now implements dart string childpath string name if segmentsabsolute final joined segments isempty name segments join name return joined final joined segments isempty name segments join name return navigatesmountnamespace projectmountsegment joined joined and extend the new direct access test with a file open upload assertion so the listing vs access namespace can t drift again |
| F2 | open | IMPORTANT | flutter_app/lib/ui/widgets/wide_layout_shell.dart | ⚠️ important recent folder chips bypass the allow access gate on sandboxed hosts the pr scopes direct access to non sandboxed hosts non sandbox hosts open session folders directly no gate and keeps the filessessionfoldergate allow access flow for folders a sandboxed env cannot open the chip path doesn t respect that split resolvefilesenv roots the files env directly at the folder via createfolderenv recentfolder with no grant and no directfolderaccess check on a sandboxed host macos app store build ios with a bookmarked folder outside the container 1 createfolderenv path → localexecutionenv cwd path — un granted folder 2 sessionfolder recentfolder wide layout shell dart 2532 2555 makes gatedsessionfolder return null because visiblefolderroot matches the candidate against env cwd project mount flow dart 110 — the folder now is the cwd so the gate never renders even though the env cannot read it 3 listdir fails with the sandbox permission error the user sees could not list folder where the pre pr flow offered the allow access picker which per this same pr now opens at the folder — one click to grant a previously mounted chat folder is exactly the recents entry that hits this and it is the case the gate exists for suggest either gating the re root on the same seam the browser uses dart future executionenv resolvefilesenv string recentfolder final service widget manager active service final direct visiblefolderroot service env await resolvehomeenv recentfolder null or expose directfolderaccess return recentfolder null direct createfolderenv recentfolder …existing… non direct keep the gate flow don t set sessionfolder re root or reusing pickandapplyprojectmount initialpath recentfolder for the non direct case so the grant persist path stays in one place a test pumping the chip tap with debugdirectfolderaccess false would pin the contract the new tests only cover the direct path |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

