## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F3 | open | IMPORTANT | flutter_app/lib/ui/screens/app_launcher_screen.dart | ⚠️ important launcher chip route still unpinned — the sandbox gate regression covers only the shell surface the f2 fix is correct on both routes verified in source resolvefilesenv wide layout shell dart 2590 and resolverecentfilesenv app launcher screen dart 1083 now consult the shared directfolderaccessallowed seam but the delivered regression — wide layout shell actions test dart sandbox recent folder chip preserves the allow access gate — exercises only the shell route no test pumps a chip tap through the launcher route with debugdirectfolderaccess false the launcher surface is live code not a stub the shell hosts applauncherscreen with filesrecentfolders recentchatfolders wide layout shell dart 1780 the files tile opens the launcher files route with recents app launcher screen dart 1106 and every chip tap funnels through openfilesat → resolverecentfilesenv the gate decision therefore exists as a second independently maintained copy of the exact logic that already regressed once the original pr wrote createfolderenv path unconditionally here which masked the allow access gate behind a bare listing error — precisely what f2 was raised for a future simplification of this helper would silently re break the gate on the launcher surface and the shell test would stay green test app launcher screen test dart already has the harness for this files tile pushes the file browser mirroring the shell regression there — provide filesrecentfolders tap the files tile tap a chip with debugdirectfolderaccess false assert filessessionfoldergate renders and could not list folder does not — pins both copies of the contract f2 s own thread asked for exactly this pin it landed for one of the two chip surfaces |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

